-- title:
--   Regularity of the special fibre along the ∞-chart, q=3
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q=3$, let $M'\ge 1$ with $q\nmid M'$, and let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero, algebraic over $\mathbb Q$, containing a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$ such that some ring homomorphism $\iota:L\to\mathbb C$ sends $\zeta$ to $e^{2\pi i/q}$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L\subseteq L((T))$ generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise image, under $\mathbb Q\to L$, of the $q$-expansion function field of the modular curve of level $q^2M'$ attached to the subgroup $H\le(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$ which is the kernel of reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $q$ in its maximal ideal, with $\zeta$ in the image of $A\to L$, with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with the tower $A\to L\to K$, and let $\varpi$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $j\in K$ be nonzero with image in $L((T))$ the coefficientwise image of the rational $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) $=T^{-1}\cdot$`jNumQ`. Let $W_0$ be a valuation subring of $K$ consisting exactly of those $f$ for which there are power series $x,y$ over $A$ with $y$ nonzero modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ and $f\cdot y=x$ in $L((T))$ after mapping coefficients to $L$. Let $\mathfrak X=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout over `XMid` of the two spectra of the integral closures of $A[j]$ and of $A[j^{-1}]$ in $K$, and let $z\in\mathfrak X$. Let $\varpi_z$ be the image of $\varpi$ in the stalk at $z$ under the structure morphism $\mathfrak X\to\operatorname{Spec}A$ followed by the germ map at $z$, and assume $\varpi_z$ lies in the maximal ideal of that stalk. Assume $z$ is not in the image on points of the morphism `ιFin` from the $j$-finite chart, and that for every prime $y$ of the integral closure of $A[j^{-1}]$ in $K$ with `ιInf` image $z$, every element of that integral closure which, viewed in $K$, is a nonunit of $W_0$ lies in $y$. Then the quotient of the stalk of $\mathfrak X$ at $z$ by the ideal generated by $\varpi_z$ is a regular local ring.
--
--   This is the $q=3$ case of the statement that the special fibre of the two-chart integral model of the modular curve of level $q^2M'$ with $H$ the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$ is regular at the points of the branch cut out by the Gauss valuation $W_0$ which do not lie on the $j$-finite chart. It feeds the construction of an open subscheme smooth over the base and the corresponding regularity statement at good points of the two-chart model.
